speechtext:
Then the matter becomes more complex still, because how can the pools arrive at the amount available for distribution except by adding up the claims of the several
12739-106}
primary producers on a rateable basis and advising the government that Alberta requires so much, Saskatchewan so much and Manitoba so much? But the minister says that the claim will amount to 86,509,000 and there is 891,000 leeway. They add it up to make the distribution; if the expenses are 891,000 no part of it can come out of that; the expenses have to come out of the amount payable to the primary producers. That is clear from the terms of this section. The minister has said that there is no sum for expenses to be paid by the government; he said that over and over again-
